      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-109156",
      ":question/problem": "If $x=5{y}^{3}-10{y}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-10\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =15{y}^{2}-20y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}\\right)}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-20y}.\n$$"
